  With all my great respect to Nick Szabo's ideas on the Future
of Science  I can't help  noticing  that  most of the topics he
describes refer to Technology, not Science.
   It seems only natural that with passage of time,  one moves
from learning the Rules of the Game to playing the Game itself.
The civilization is maturing.
   I would expect that  eventually  technology will take most of
the effort, while most of science will be directed at studies of
methods of development and the current status of achievements.
This transition has already happened  in some disciplines,  like
geography, mechanics, etc., and is gradually happening in others
(chemistry, geology, economics,...).
   
 [  The laws  governing the behavior  of systems  that have never
